{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/005-continue.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"command\":\"story-continue\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"4d424e88-0a49-49ce-a308-fff2776e4b7d\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"28aec8fc-3297-4f03-8488-65ebfbadd697\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"28aec8fc-3297-4f03-8488-65ebfbadd697\",\"storyId\":\"01-pull-and-status\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-pull-and-status\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Pull and Status on the Record\"},\"planSummary\":\"Fixed SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001 at the seam layer: the verified side-effect path was openThreadDatabase → fireThreadTouch → scheduler.touch, which in a background SDK can hang a first-touch catch-up drain (queue claims, provider calls, writes) off a thread-view read. The fix is a reads-only operation scope in shared/context.ts — runWithThreadTouchSuppressed runs a function under the current instance seam with the touch announcement replaced by a no-op while preserving the poke target and view config (and delegating to the below-SDK defaults when no seam is in scope, minus the touch). thread-view pull and status wrap their entire bodies in this scope, which structurally covers not just their own openThreadDatabase calls but also the owners' report surfaces status consumes — no test-only bypass, no signature changes to the frozen messages/turns domains, and write paths are untouched so first-touch catch-up still works everywhere it should. A new background-mode test leg extends TC-1.2/TC-2.5: pending work is manufactured through a manual SDK, then a fresh background SDK pulls twice and reads status; it asserts work rows / form states / view rows / boundary unchanged (full below-SDK state snapshot), provider fake at zero calls, repeated pulls byte-identical via full-result hash, repeated status byte-identical, and pending work visible through the read itself — after settling the scheduler (timeout + drainSettled) so a wrongly-scheduled drain would surface. The regression test was proven live: with the suppression temporarily removed it fails (the catch-up drain fires), with the fix it passes.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"reason\":\"New runWithThreadTouchSuppressed: reads-only operation scope that suppresses the DD-10 open announcement under the current seam (poke and view config carried through; below-SDK fallback preserved minus touch)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"pull and status bodies run inside the touch-suppressed scope so AC-1.1/AC-2.8 reads-only holds structurally in both host modes, covering their own opens and status's report-surface opens\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"New background-leg describe extending TC-1.2/TC-2.5: background SDK with pending work — no catch-up drain, state snapshot unchanged, zero provider calls, byte-identical repeated pulls and status\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"Re-recorded view-pull.test.ts hash after the verifier-mandated test addition (strengthening only; no existing assertion weakened)\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: TC-1.2 / TC-2.5 background legs (SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001) :: schedules no catch-up drain: work rows, form states, provider count, and status all unchanged; repeated pulls byte-identical\"],\"modified\":[],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":244,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":16},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001: background-mode threadView.pull/status no longer fire the thread-touch announcement, so the scheduler's first-touch catch-up drain can never be scheduled by a read; verified by a regression test that fails when the suppression is removed and passes with it.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"The suppression is scoped to the thread-view ops, not to openThreadDatabase generally: other read surfaces (messages.listMessages, reports called directly) still announce opens, preserving Epic 02's first-touch catch-up behavior — only the Epic 03 reads carry the reads-only contract. If a later story wants all reads touch-free, the same scope function is the seam to apply.\",\"openThreadDatabase still runs schema migrations on a pre-current-version file during pull/status (existing every-operation contract from Epic 01); the finding's queue/provider/write classes are closed, but a first open of a legacy file remains a schema write by design.\",\"test/view-pull.test.ts was modified after its Red-manifest recording solely to ADD the verifier-mandated background legs; the manifest hash was re-recorded and no existing assertion was weakened.\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Re-run story verification for SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001 closure; Story 2 (compact) can proceed on the unchanged array-shape contract.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/005-continue.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T15:03:07.276Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T15:06:38.634Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
